# Builder's hut (the Constructor): it invests the stone in its stock into the nearest own-team blueprint or damaged
# structure within "Constructor range". A 1x1 PYLON TOWER as tall as a ward (3.5 m; a 1.6 x 3.5 x 1.6 m box), spawned
# origin 1.75 above the ground.
# SHAPE (a placeholder; uniform scales of the baseshapes variants): a stone plinth (the root), a pale stone drum, a
# shaft on it, a violet slate ledge on top and the floating HEAD over it. The child pieces are render-only.
# THE HEAD turns to the work (StructureSystem::poseAimHeads, from Ref::headYaw; "Constructor turn speed (deg/s)"): its
# local +X is the aim. A violet focus crystal lying along +X and one small stone floating behind it (so the back reads).
# The stone stream starts at the crystal's point (keep the `Head` height and the crystal's length in step with
# c_crystalHeight / c_crystalTip in StructureSystem::drawBuilderStreams, Game/Private/StructuresEconomy.cpp).
Prefab gameConstructor
	Global true
	Component Render
		ObjectContainer baseshapes
		Node CubeQuarter
		Type StaticMesh
		Color 0.45 0.45 0.5
		Position 0 -1.51 0
		Scale 0.95
	Component Physics
		Body Static
		ContactEvents true
		Shape Box
		HalfExtents 0.8 1.75 0.8
	Component GameStructure
		MeleeRadius 1
